      "body": "# [Fix] Lazy-load SM100-only GDN BF16-state kernel so FlashInfer GDN works on Hopper\n\n## Motivation\n\nFixes #32063.\n\n`_get_flashinfer_gdn_kernels()` unconditionally imports\n`flashinfer.gdn_kernels.gdn_decode_bf16_state` inside the try/except that\ndecides backend availability. That module is CuTe-DSL based\n(`import cutlass` at module level) and is **only consumed on SM100+**\n(`use_state_pool = sm_major >= 10`; SM90 uses fp32 state per the module\ndocstring).\n\nOn Hopper installs without the DSL dependencies (e.g. flashinfer 0.6.12\nwheel without `nvidia-cutlass-dsl`), the import raises\n`ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'cutlass'`, the availability check\nswallows it, and the **entire FlashInfer GDN backend is silently disabled\non SM90** — even though every kernel SM90 actually uses imported fine.\nLaunching with `--linear-attn-prefill-backend flashinfer` then fails with a\nmisleading \"Requires SM90+\" error.\n\n## Modifications\n\nImport the BF16-state MTP kernel only on SM100+, defaulting the symbol to\n`None` otherwise (the consumer side already handles `mtp_bf16_fn is None`\nand is additionally gated by `use_state_pool`):\n\n```python\n            gated_delta_rule_mtp_bf16 = None\n            if is_cuda() and torch.cuda.get_device_capability()[0] >= 10:\n                from flashinfer.gdn_kernels.gdn_decode_bf16_state import (\n                    gated_delta_rule_mtp as gated_delta_rule_mtp_bf16,\n                )\n```\n\n- SM90 (Hopper): backend availability now depends only on the SM90 kernels;\n  decode / prefill / MTP behavior unchanged (they never used the BF16-state\n  kernel).\n- SM100+ (Blackwell): unchanged — the kernel is still imported inside the\n  same try/except, so a broken DSL install degrades availability exactly as\n  before.\n\n## Verification\n\n- On 8x H800 (SM90), flashinfer 0.6.12 without `cutlass`: before the fix,\n  the backend was unavailable; after the fix, \"FlashInfer GDN kernels\n  loaded successfully\" and Qwen3.5-397B-A17B-FP8 runs end-to-end with\n  `--linear-attn-prefill-backend flashinfer` (outputs match the triton\n  linear-attn backend baseline).\n- `FlashInferGDNKernel` init path re-checked: `mtp_bf16_fn is None` is\n  already handled and the bf16 adapter is gated by `use_state_pool`.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code with pre-commit.\n- [x] Verified end-to-end as described above.\n- [x] Update documentation as needed. (N/A)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #30358398840](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30358398840)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #30358398701](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/30358398701)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
